  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find the values of $x$ for which:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q5a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1x\\le4x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac12\\le x<0$ or $x\\ge\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, multiply by $x^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x&\\le4x^3\\\\4x^3-x&\\ge0\\\\x(2x-1)(2x+1)&\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe cubic is non-negative on $[-\\frac12,0]$ and $[\\frac12,\\infty)$. Exclude $x=0$: $-\\frac12\\le x<0$ or $x\\ge\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q5b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2}{x-4}>18$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4<x<6$ or $x>12$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne4$, multiply by $(x-4)^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2(x-4)&>18(x-4)^2\\\\(x-4)(x^2-18x+72)&>0\\\\(x-4)(x-6)(x-12)&>0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe cubic is positive for $4<x<6$ and $x>12$. Hence $4<x<6$ or $x>12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q5c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x}<3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-1$ or $0<x<4$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, multiply by $x^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x^2-4)&<3x^2\\\\x^3-3x^2-4x&<0\\\\x(x-4)(x+1)&<0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe cubic is negative for $x<-1$ and $0<x<4$. Thus $x<-1$ or $0<x<4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q5d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x^2-9}\\le0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-3<x\\le-2$ or $2\\le x<3$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\pm3$, multiply by $(x^2-9)^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^2-4)(x^2-9)&\\le0\\\\(x-2)(x+2)(x-3)(x+3)&\\le0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe quartic is non-positive on $[-3,-2]$ and $[2,3]$. Exclude the undefined values $\\pm3$: $-3<x\\le-2$ or $2\\le x<3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q5e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x^2-4}<1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-2$ or $x>2$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\pm2$, multiply by $(x^2-4)^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^2-9)(x^2-4)&<(x^2-4)^2\\\\(x^2-4)[(x^2-9)-(x^2-4)]&<0\\\\-5(x^2-4)&<0\\\\x^2-4&>0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe upward-opening graph is positive outside its zeroes. Hence $x<-2$ or $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q5f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x+\\dfrac2x\\ge3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0<x\\le1$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, multiply by $x^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3+2x&\\ge3x^2\\\\x^3-3x^2+2x&\\ge0\\\\x(x-1)(x-2)&\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe cubic is non-negative on $[0,1]$ and $[2,\\infty)$. Exclude $x=0$: $0<x\\le1$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
